From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bjakra <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:15:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pan/kmod, panfrost: let a backend own sync objects, job
 submission and imports

The gallium driver called libdrm for its sync objects and sent
DRM_IOCTL_PANFROST_SUBMIT itself, and pan_kmod imported a BO by turning a
dma-buf into a GEM handle, all of which ties the job manager path to a DRM
kernel driver. Make them optional backend hooks: creating, destroying,
waiting for and copying a sync object, submitting a job chain, importing
the memory behind a file descriptor and mapping a BO on the CPU. libdrm
and the ioctls remain what happens when a backend has none, so nothing
changes for panfrost and panthor.

pan_kmod_dev_is_drm() says which kind a device is. Where it is not DRM
there are no sync files: fences are not exported or imported
(native_fence_fd is off), the screen has no DRM fd to hand out, BOs are
not exported, and import is offered if the backend has the hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A7tdbX9rySEX8PF9LVaYr5
